# The app stores your account's portfolio in MongoDB through the
# resume-analyzer backend. React Native cannot open a MongoDB connection
# itself — the driver needs Node TCP sockets — so everything server-side goes
# over HTTP to that backend.
#
# In development the API host is derived automatically from the Metro host, so
# a phone on the same Wi-Fi finds the backend on port 5000 with no config.
# Set this only to point somewhere else (a deployed backend, a different port).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.5:5000

# --- Google sign-in ---------------------------------------------------------
# Create OAuth client IDs at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# (one per platform you build for), then put the same values in the backend's
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS so it trusts those audiences.
#
# Google sign-in also needs two packages that are not installed yet:
#   npx expo install expo-auth-session expo-web-browser expo-crypto
# expo-web-browser is a native module, so the dev client must be rebuilt after
# installing it. See src/lib/auth/googleSignIn.ts.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
